ame to you...well ok, that's not necessarily true. Everyone does have to eat though. Nothing's going to change that. Why not embrace that truth rather than suffering in humane martyrdom. That's a lifestyle choice. Hunger isn't.<br /> <br /> Celebrants, Nightmares as Legacy: Here's the thing about dreams and nightmares, they're fleeting. Try remembering the last dream you had. Last nightmare? No? That's not a suprise. Dreams are fleeting because life is fleeting. We're born, live our lives for as long as we can, and then die. It doesn't have to be that way though. A part of one's self can survive beyond the veil of death. Shape the lives of countless humans and more. The dream need not die with the dreamer, nor the nightmare. The Legend holds the seeds of immortality. The Primordial Dream is shaped by the ancient shadows of monsters and fiends long gone, but who's actions and deeds still haunt the dreams of mortal minds. The hunger pushes one towards apotheosis, to a state of divinity impossible to obtain through mortal means. Follow the footsteps of those who devoured before you. Seek to become the Incarnant Beast. Become Myth, else all you are pass into eternity with the rising sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like this idea, perhaps even more than the concept of Hungers. Hopefully we can get something like this as the &quot;augment X-splat/Y-splat&quot; option down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T16:21:35-07:00","id":924165,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that one aspect I don't think I've yet seen is Beasts As Reflection. The text is so focused on family with all the other monsters that it seems to forget that humans can be the biggest monsters of all. Maybe most people will never have a direct connection to a Horror, but they don't need that to do many of the objectionable things Beasts do. The Horror makes it easier, sure, but it was always possible. I can see Beasts saying &quot;I'm you, just with more power and less restraint, and deep down you know it.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's sort of a theme of the CoD as a whole, looking at human problems and shortcomings from a perspective just outside human, but as the crossover splat I think Beast has potential to really dig into it. The Kinship nightmares are a start, looking into what human fear each monster specifically represents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}